# Walkthrough - Timetable Dynamic Vertical Expansion

I have updated the timetable to allow slots to expand vertically to accommodate long text while staying strictly within their grid zones.

## Changes Made

### Frontend

#### [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx)
- **Removed line-clamping**: Removed `line-clamp-2` and `md:line-clamp-3` from module names and event descriptions. All text will now be visible.
- **Dynamic Grid Height**: Changed the horizontal timetable cells from fixed `h-[110px]` to `min-h-[110px] h-auto`. This allows rows to expand vertically if a slot's content is long.
- **Grid Integrity**: Slots remain strictly within their day (horizontal rows) and time (vertical columns) zones. If one slot expands, the entire row for that day expands, maintaining the visual alignment of the grid.

## Verification Results

### Visual Inspection
- Verified that slots with long module names now expand the row height instead of hiding text.
- Confirmed that "CS2030 Recitation" (or any other slot) stays within its day row and time column.
- The layout remains responsive and interactive, with hover effects scaling correctly to the new dynamic heights.
